    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "3.9 inches sounds like a lot of movement though, isn't it? if i'm actually trying to prevent that \"bouncy\" feeling for people walking around up there, shouldn't i be aiming for the tighter end of that spec? also, you mentioned looking for knots or defects. besides the obvious stuff like big cracks or rot, are there any subtle, hidden issues inside the wood that i might miss just by looking at the surface? i want to make sure there aren't any structural weaknesses tucked away where i can't see 'em.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
