      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that $L/360$ is very conservative for perceived comfort, so aiming for the tighter $L/240$ limit is wise for eliminating bounce. Regarding hidden flaws, deep checking or internal decay is a serious concern, as is internal checking or splitting along the grain that isn't easily visible from the end. While visual inspection is crucial, samples should ideally be tested or, in critical areas, non-destructive testing might be warranted to confirm uniform density and absence of hidden infestation.",
